== The Three Source Implementations ==

=== Implementation 1: Biological Source ===

From [[Psionics]] (Wilson–Cowan coupling):

:<math>J_\psi^{\rm (bio)}(\mathbf{x},t) \propto \int f\!\bigl(u(\mathbf{x}',t)\bigr)\,d^3x'</math>

where <math>f(u)</math> is the neural firing rate in the Wilson–Cowan model. The biological source is:
* '''Spatial extent:''' distributed over the cortex, primarily temporal and frontal lobes during coherent states
* '''Temporal character:''' oscillating at the operator's coherence frequency <math>\omega_{\rm bio}</math> (related to alpha/theta EEG band via the ψ–EM coupling)
* '''Amplitude:''' proportional to RMSSD; increases with HRV coherence training

The biological source is Track B — its existence and magnitude are the primary TML-3 measurement targets.

=== Implementation 2: Electromagnetic Device Source ===

From [[ψ Transducer]] (C3):

:<math>J_\psi^{\rm (dev)}(\mathbf{x},t) = \alpha\,\varepsilon_{\rm eff}(V(t))\,E^2_{\rm bifilar}(\mathbf{x},t)</math>

The device source is:
* '''Spatial extent:''' concentrated at the bifilar trace gap volume within the TPMS lattice
* '''Temporal character:''' driven at <math>\omega_{\rm drive}</math> by the [[Shepard Tone Synthesis]] (D2) waveform
* '''Amplitude:''' proportional to drive voltage squared and BST permittivity
* '''Track:''' Track A (buildable now) — the EM source term exists regardless of whether ψ is real

=== Implementation 3: Hybrid Source ===

Total source:

:<math>J_\psi^{\rm (total)} = J_\psi^{\rm (dev)} + J_\psi^{\rm (bio)}</math>

For constructive superposition at the temporal lobe target:

:<math>\text{arg}(G * J_\psi^{\rm (dev)}) = \text{arg}(G * J_\psi^{\rm (bio)}) \quad \text{at } \mathbf{x}_{\rm temporal}</math>

This phase-matching condition is implemented by the [[HRV-Gated Drive]] (D5) Mk2.0 loop — the device source phase is continuously adjusted to remain in phase with the biological source. When matched, total source amplitude = device + biological; when mismatched, partial or complete cancellation occurs.

== Source Strength and Radiation Efficiency ==

The ψ field at the target location (temporal lobes) is computed from the design convolution (A6):

:<math>\psi(\mathbf{x}_{\rm target}) = \int G_{\rm ret}(\mathbf{x}_{\rm target},\mathbf{x}')\,J_\psi^{\rm (total)}(\mathbf{x}')\,d^4x'</math>

The radiation efficiency — fraction of total source power that reaches the target:

:<math>\eta_{\rm rad} = \frac{|\psi(\mathbf{x}_{\rm target})|^2}{||J_\psi^{\rm (total)}||^2} \cdot \frac{1}{|G(\mathbf{x}_{\rm target},\mathbf{x}')|^2_{\rm mean}}</math>

This efficiency is maximised when the source spatial distribution is matched to the Green's function — i.e., when the source is concentrated where the Green's function has its maximum. For the [[ψ Resonator]] cavity at resonance, the Green's function is dominated by the ψ₀₁₀ mode shape, so the optimal source distribution is proportional to <math>\psi_{010}(\mathbf{x}')</math> — exactly the bifilar coil pattern optimisation from C3.

