== ψ-Dependent Extensions ==

=== α Measurement as Critical Calibration ===

The device source strength <math>J_\psi^{\rm (dev)} = \alpha\varepsilon_{\rm eff}E^2_{\rm bif}</math> depends on the coupling constant <math>\alpha</math>, which is unmeasured. Until <math>\alpha</math> is measured at TML-3, the device source strength cannot be computed in absolute units — only relative changes (from BST bias or drive voltage variation) are predictable.

The first TML-3 measurement goal is therefore to constrain <math>\alpha</math> by comparing the device source strength (known in EM units) to the biological effect size (measured in RMSSD units) via the theoretical transfer function from the master equation. This is the single most important experimental result in the entire Psionic Engineering programme.

